<p>In this example the savings nearly disappear because the FSBO seller contributes to the buyer's agent and sells a little below market. If you sell to an unrepresented buyer and price well, FSBO saves much more. If you misprice or a deal falls apart, it can cost more. Run both scenarios in the <a href="/tools/seller-net-proceeds-calculator/">seller net proceeds calculator</a>.</p>

<h2>Bottom line</h2>
<p>Selling a house by owner in Texas works best when you price from real market data, complete the seller's disclosure notice before listing, use the current TREC forms with an attorney's review, and close through a title company. Decide up front how you will handle buyer-agent compensation under the 2024 settlement and Texas's 2026 written-agreement law. Then judge every offer by what you actually net.</p>
